# Jobby — container configuration
#
# ── Quick start (Docker Compose: web + worker + redis) ───────────────────────
#   cp deploy/.env.example deploy/.env          # deploy/.env is gitignored
#   # fill AUTH_SECRET, JOBBY_OPERATOR_SECRET, JOBBY_MASTER_KEY (see table)
#   # set JOBBY_HOST_ROOT to this checkout's absolute path (output of `pwd`)
#   docker compose -f deploy/docker-compose.yml --env-file deploy/.env up -d --build
#   open http://localhost:4700  → "Operator sign-in" with JOBBY_OPERATOR_SECRET
#   docker compose -f deploy/docker-compose.yml logs -f web     # logs
#   docker compose -f deploy/docker-compose.yml down            # stop
#
# The repo root is bind-mounted at /data (CAREER_OPS_ROOT): your cv.md,
# config/profile.yml, portals.yml and data/ live on the host, not in the image.
# Code changes need `up --build`; there is no hot reload inside the container.
#
# ── Tokens / secrets ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Never commit deploy/.env. Every value below is yours to generate or obtain.
#
#   Variable               Required  What it is / how to get it
#   AUTH_SECRET            yes       Signs session cookies. `npx auth secret`
#                                    or `openssl rand -base64 32`.
#   JOBBY_OPERATOR_SECRET  yes       Password for the "Operator sign-in" (admin).
#                                    `openssl rand -base64 24`. Without it the
#                                    operator door is shown as not configured.
#   JOBBY_MASTER_KEY       yes       Encrypts every user's stored AI keys at rest.
#                                    `openssl rand -base64 32`. Losing or changing
#                                    it makes stored keys undecryptable — back it up.
#   AUTH_URL               yes       Exact origin users open (http://localhost:4700
#                                    or your public https URL). Mismatch = login loop.
#   OPENROUTER_API_KEY     no        Operator AI key for scoring (openrouter.ai →
#                                    Keys). Also OPENAI_/ANTHROPIC_/GEMINI_API_KEY.
#                                    Ignored when AUTH_SINGLE_TENANT=0: each user
#                                    pastes their own key in Config.
#   AUTH_GITHUB_ID/SECRET  no        GitHub OAuth app (Settings → Developer settings
#   AUTH_GOOGLE_ID/SECRET            → OAuth Apps; callback {AUTH_URL}/api/auth/
#                                    callback/github). Google: Cloud Console OAuth.
#   APPWRITE_ENDPOINT,     no*       Appwrite project (cloud.appwrite.io or self-
#   APPWRITE_PROJECT_ID,             hosted). Server API key with databases + users
#   APPWRITE_API_KEY                 scopes. Enables email sign-up, accounts, MCP
#                                    keys, usage caps. *Needed for multi-user.
#                                    Create schema: node scripts/appwrite-schema.mjs
#   JOBBY_OMNIROUTE_*      no        Only if you run an OpenAI-compatible gateway
#                                    for the in-container OpenCode CLI.
#
# MCP keys (`jb_…`) are NOT env vars: each user mints them in the UI
# (Config → MCP), they are shown once and stored hashed. Treat one like a
# password; revoke it in the UI if it leaks.
#
# ── Single user vs shared ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
# AUTH_SINGLE_TENANT=1  one person, local machine, operator sign-in only.
# AUTH_SINGLE_TENANT=0  anyone else can reach it: configure Appwrite and/or OAuth.
#
# ── Exposing it (optional) ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The web port binds 127.0.0.1 only (JOBBY_BIND_ADDR). To reach it remotely put
# HTTPS in front (Tailscale Funnel, Cloudflare Tunnel, reverse proxy) pointing at
# http://127.0.0.1:${JOBBY_WEB_PORT}, then set AUTH_URL and JOBBY_MCP_PUBLIC_URL
# to that https origin. Tailscale example:
#   tailscale funnel --bg --https=443 http://127.0.0.1:4700
#   AUTH_URL=https://<machine>.<tailnet>.ts.net  (MCP: <same>/mcp/jb_…)
# Redis is never published.
#
# Railway: set the same keys on web + worker services; add Redis plugin → REDIS_URL.

# Auth.js (JOBBY-BL-020). Generate: npx auth secret
# AUTH_URL must match the host URL (JOBBY_WEB_PORT / .ports.yml compose-web).
AUTH_SECRET=
# 1 = every sign-in shares the `default` tenant (correct ONLY for a single-user
# local install). Set 0 for any instance more than one person can reach, or the
# app refuses to boot once GitHub/Google sign-in is configured.
AUTH_SINGLE_TENANT=1
JOBBY_OPERATOR_SECRET=

# Master key that encrypts every tenant's stored provider keys (JOBBY-BL-021).
# REQUIRED in production — the app fails closed without it, because inventing one
# at boot would make yesterday's stored keys undecryptable after a restart.
# Generate: openssl rand -base64 32
JOBBY_MASTER_KEY=
# Cipher backend for that master key: `local` (node:crypto) today; OpenBao/Vault
# Transit or a cloud KMS plug in behind the same interface.
# JOBBY_KEY_BACKEND=local

# Optional OAuth (leave empty to hide those buttons). Requires AUTH_SINGLE_TENANT=0.
# AUTH_GITHUB_ID=
# AUTH_GITHUB_SECRET=
# AUTH_GOOGLE_ID=
# AUTH_GOOGLE_SECRET=
# AUTH_ALLOWED_EMAILS=you@example.com
# NEXT_PUBLIC_AUTH_GITHUB=1
# NEXT_PUBLIC_AUTH_GOOGLE=1

# Appwrite (accounts, email sign-up, MCP keys, usage caps). See table above.
# APPWRITE_ENDPOINT=https://cloud.appwrite.io/v1
# APPWRITE_PROJECT_ID=
# APPWRITE_API_KEY=

# After a user deletes their account there is a 7-day grace window, then:
#   node scripts/account-lifecycle.mjs purge-expired
# JOBBY_ACCOUNT_GRACE_MS=604800000

# Shared
CAREER_OPS_ROOT=/data
REDIS_URL=redis://redis:6379
JOBBY_ALLOW_API_KEY=1
# LinkedIn Explore / scan.mjs JobSpy. Compose images set this to /opt/jobspy/bin/python.
# Host `npm run dev`: create `.venv-jobspy` or point this at a python with python-jobspy.
# JOBBY_JOBSPY_PYTHON=/opt/jobspy/bin/python

# Host publish port — must match .ports.yml services.compose-web. Container Next is always :3000.
JOBBY_WEB_PORT=4700
AUTH_URL=http://localhost:4700

# API-key scoring (second engine — Config "Paste an AI key" / cliId=openrouter).
# These are IGNORED when AUTH_SINGLE_TENANT=0: on a shared instance every tenant
# brings their own key through Config, so one operator key cannot fund everyone.
OPENROUTER_API_KEY=
# Optional: pin OpenRouter model for Score quality (free tier rotates otherwise)
# CAREER_OPS_MODEL=meta-llama/llama-3.3-70b-instruct:free
# OPENAI_API_KEY=
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
# GEMINI_API_KEY=

# Optional model pins for in-container CLIs
# JOBBY_CLAUDE_MODEL=sonnet
# JOBBY_CURSOR_MODEL=composer-2.5-fast
# Host Ollama from containers (default in compose):
JOBBY_OLLAMA_BASE_URL=http://host.docker.internal:11434/v1
# JOBBY_OLLAMA_MODEL=qwen3:8b
# OpenCode in-container: same OmniRoute gateway as host ~/.config/opencode/opencode.json
OPENCODE_MODEL=omniroute/auto/best-coding
JOBBY_OMNIROUTE_BASE_URL=https://your-gateway.your-tailnet.ts.net:8443/v1
JOBBY_OMNIROUTE_API_KEY=
#
# CLIs in the container image (by design):
#   ✅ OpenCode  — baked into Dockerfile.web + Dockerfile.worker
#   ✅ OpenRouter — API key (no CLI binary)
#   ❌ Claude / Codex / Cursor / Gemini / Copilot / Qwen / Antigravity
#      Not baked (license, size, interactive login). Use host `npm run dev` /
#      `web` outside Docker if you need those, or stick to OpenCode/OpenRouter.

# Scan caps (members). Operator is uncapped. Written to Appwrite usage_events.
# Plan table in SYSTEM.md is the default; these override for tests.
# JOBBY_SCAN_DAILY_LIMIT=5
# JOBBY_MCP_DAILY_LIMIT=40
# JOBBY_SCAN_CONCURRENCY=1
# JOBBY_SCAN_LOCK_STALE_MS=1200000

# Shared dispatcher sandbox slots. Default 1. Raise only when the production host has
# spare CPU/RAM. Isolation is per job (tenant mount + key), not per account.
# Score fairness (1 running + 1 waiting per tenant) still holds at 3.
# JOBBY_WORKER_CONCURRENCY=1

# Per-job sandbox (dispatcher holds the Docker socket; sandboxes do not).
# Absolute host path of this checkout — bind mounts are resolved on the host.
# Required: compose refuses to start without it. Compose does not expand ${PWD}.
JOBBY_HOST_ROOT=/absolute/path/to/jobby
# JOBBY_SANDBOX=1
# JOBBY_SANDBOX_IMAGE=jobby-worker:local
# JOBBY_SANDBOX_NETWORK=jobby_sandbox
# JOBBY_SANDBOX_MEMORY=2g
# JOBBY_SANDBOX_CPUS=2
# JOBBY_SANDBOX_TIMEOUT_MS=900000

# Scheduler profile: docker compose --profile scheduler -f deploy/docker-compose.yml up
# JOBBY_SCAN_CRON=0 */6 * * *

# Railway notes:
# - Create project with services: web (Dockerfile.web), worker (Dockerfile.worker), Redis plugin
# - Root directory / build context = repo root; Dockerfile path = deploy/Dockerfile.*
# - POC is local-first: bind-mount or sync CAREER_OPS_ROOT; remote Railway without a volume is stateless for user data
# - Smoke: open /config → pick OpenCode or openrouter → Save → Score one URL from Pipeline

# --- Network exposure (M7 phase 5) ---
# Which host address the web container publishes on. Loopback by default, so the
# app does NOT answer the local network. Tailscale Funnel and Cloudflare proxy
# from this machine, so they work unchanged. To serve the tailnet directly, put
# this host's tailnet address here (100.x.y.z) — never 0.0.0.0.
JOBBY_BIND_ADDR=127.0.0.1

# Public HTTPS origin for ChatGPT / claude.ai MCP. No port — those clients
# reject :8443. Funnel :443 /mcp|/api/mcp|/sse|/.well-known →
# http://127.0.0.1:<compose-web> from .ports.yml (not :3001).
# :443 / is OmniRoute. See .cursor/skills/tailscale-serve/SKILL.md.
# Example: https://your-machine.tailxxxxx.ts.net
# JOBBY_MCP_PUBLIC_URL=https://your-machine.tailxxxxx.ts.net

# Public origin for Jobby dashboard deep links in MCP job tables (links.jobby).
# Use the URL where you open the web UI (AUTH_URL locally, or your tunnel/domain).
# JOBBY_APP_PUBLIC_URL=https://jobby.yourdomain.com

# Redis is deliberately not published at all: it has no password and holds the
# job queue, so anyone who can reach it can enqueue work into another account's
# directory. There is no variable to expose it.
